  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ajay Ashok Lodhi vs State Of Maharashtra on 13 October, 2023 Author: M. S. Karnik Bench: M. S. Karnik 2023:Bhc-As:30651 Diksha Rane 933. Ba 2972-23.d In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Bail Application No.2972/2023 Ajay Ashok Lodhi ..Applicant Vs. The State Of Maharashtra ..Respondent ------------ Adv. Anuj Tiwari a/w. Adv. Rahil Kazi for the applicant. Ms. Rutuja Ambekar, App for the State. ------------ Coram : M. S. Karnik, J. Date : October 13, 2023. P.C. : 1.",
    "facts": "While on patrolling duty on 8/7/2023, the complainant received confidential information that a tempo wa Diksha Rane 933. BA 2972-23.doc transporting prohibited food items namely Pan Masala and scented tobacco. The vehicle was stopped near H.A.L. township gate no.3, at 2.30 p.m. It was found that the vehicle was carrying 30 gunny bags containing 570 packets of Pan Masala and scented tobacco in each bag. It was later revealed that the said goods were transported from Indore. The applicant is from Indore. During the course of the raid in the godown, the applicant was found, from where he was arrested. 4. It is the prosecution case that the applicant is the manager of the main accused who owns the godown and these products. Learned APP opposed the application and submitted that huge quantity of banned product was found. 5. The issue whether the contraband would be covered by Section 328 of the IPC is pending before the Hon'ble Supreme Court. The applicant was arrested on 13/7/2023 and now is in custody for almost three months with no possibility of the trial concluding any time soon. The investigation is complete. The charge-sheet has been filed. There are no criminal antecedents reported against the applicant.",
